Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Common/Math: fix the scalar LoadF24x4 fallback

The no-SIMD branch of CrossSIMD.h called LoadR24x3_One, which does not
exist anywhere in the tree — LoadF24x3_One does. The branch only compiles
on a target with neither SSE nor NEON, which is why it has gone unnoticed.

Correcting the name alone would compile and be wrong: the SSE and NEON
LoadF24x4 shift all four lanes left by 8, while LoadF24x3_One loads three
and zeroes W. This implements the four-lane semantics the other three
backends share.

diff --git a/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h b/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h
index af30c25b0..bab907de3 100644
--- a/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h
+++ b/Common/Math/CrossSIMD.h
@@ -1679,7 +1679,10 @@ struct Vec4F32 {
 	}
 
 	static Vec4F32 LoadF24x4(const uint32_t *src) {
-		return LoadR24x3_One(src);
+		uint32_t shifted[4] = { src[0] << 8, src[1] << 8, src[2] << 8, src[3] << 8 };
+		Vec4F32 temp;
+		memcpy(temp.v, shifted, sizeof(temp.v));
+		return temp;
 	}
 
 	static Vec4F32 FromVec4S32(Vec4S32 src) {
